  {
    "type": "NarrativeText",
    "element_id": "c0fce57f73fa55f20d1cc8a9cd5214f9",
    "text": "Generate a new API key per user account registration",
    "metadata": {
      "languages": [
        "eng"
      ],
      "filename": "17353.txt",
      "filetype": "text/plain",
      "parent_id": "5ba5ccc6b430eb2e091dfeef1015859e",
      "data_source": {
        "url": null,
        "version": null,
        "record_locator": {
          "id": "17353",
          "key": "MAP-290",
          "board_id": null,
          "project_id": "MAP"
        },
        "date_created": null,
        "date_modified": null,
        "date_processed": "1744461415.115363",
        "permissions_data": null,
        "filesize_bytes": 3624
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "NarrativeText",
    "element_id": "eef16635854c35726d6835c73923ba6a",
    "text": "After some research this looks to be the best approach.",
    "metadata": {
      "languages": [
        "eng"
      ],
      "filename": "17353.txt",
      "filetype": "text/plain",
      "parent_id": "5ba5ccc6b430eb2e091dfeef1015859e",
      "data_source": {
        "url": null,
        "version": null,
        "record_locator": {
          "id": "17353",
          "key": "MAP-290",
          "board_id": null,
          "project_id": "MAP"
        },
        "date_created": null,
        "date_modified": null,
        "date_processed": "1744461415.115363",
        "permissions_data": null,
        "filesize_bytes": 3624
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "NarrativeText",
    "element_id": "56f3b177195c9d2953633a7b3beda35d",
    "text": "Yes, you can automatically create and associate an API key with a user as they create a new account. This is a good practice for streamlining user onboarding while maintaining individual API key management. Here's how you could approach this:",
    "metadata": {
      "languages": [
        "eng"
      ],
      "filename": "17353.txt",
      "filetype": "text/plain",
      "parent_id": "5ba5ccc6b430eb2e091dfeef1015859e",
      "data_source": {
        "url": null,
        "version": null,
        "record_locator": {
          "id": "17353",
          "key": "MAP-290",
          "board_id": null,
          "project_id": "MAP"
        },
        "date_created": null,
        "date_modified": null,
        "date_processed": "1744461415.115363",
        "permissions_data": null,
        "filesize_bytes": 3624
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "NarrativeText",
    "element_id": "be7883e5241240e0ba5de4569c73dacd",
    "text": "# User Registration Process: When a user creates a new account in your system: a. Create the user account in your database b. Make an API call to Anthropic to generate a new API key c. Associate this new API key with the user in your database d. Optionally, set up any initial usage limits or configurations for the new user # Implementation Considerations: User Registration with Anthropic API Key Generation Click to open code This example demonstrates: #* Creating a user account #* Generating an API key via Anthropic's API #* Storing the API key securely associated with the user #  Note: This is a simplified example. In a production environment, you'd want to add error handling, use environment variables for sensitive information, and possibly use asynchronous processing for API key generation. # Security Considerations: #* Never expose the full API key to the user. Store it securely on your backend. #* Use HTTPS for all communications. #* Implement proper authentication and authorization in your application. # Error Handling: #* Have a fallback plan if the API key generation fails. #* Implement retry logic for API calls to Anthropic. # Scalability: #* Consider using a job queue for API key generation if you expect high volume sign-ups. # User Management: #* Implement features to revoke, regenerate, or rotate API keys as needed. #* Provide usage statistics to users based on their individual API key.",
    "metadata": {
      "languages": [
        "eng"
      ],
      "filename": "17353.txt",
      "filetype": "text/plain",
      "parent_id": "5ba5ccc6b430eb2e091dfeef1015859e",
      "data_source": {
        "url": null,
        "version": null,
        "record_locator": {
          "id": "17353",
          "key": "MAP-290",
          "board_id": null,
          "project_id": "MAP"
        },
        "date_created": null,
        "date_modified": null,
        "date_processed": "1744461415.115363",
        "permissions_data": null,
        "filesize_bytes": 3624
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "NarrativeText",
    "element_id": "b85e6215874525d0da3008f2c930ff25",
    "text": "This approach allows you to maintain individual API keys for each user while providing a seamless onboarding experience. It gives you granular control over each user's API usage and makes it easy to manage access on a per-user basis.",
    "metadata": {
      "languages": [
        "eng"
      ],
      "filename": "17353.txt",
      "filetype": "text/plain",
      "parent_id": "5ba5ccc6b430eb2e091dfeef1015859e",
      "data_source": {
        "url": null,
        "version": null,
        "record_locator": {
          "id": "17353",
          "key": "MAP-290",
          "board_id": null,
          "project_id": "MAP"
        },
        "date_created": null,
        "date_modified": null,
        "date_processed": "1744461415.115363",
        "permissions_data": null,
        "filesize_bytes": 3624
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "Title",
    "element_id": "90949eb7169f3d1bfb9951c7b02730ad",
    "text": "Example Code -",
    "metadata": {
      "languages": [
        "eng"
      ],
      "filename": "17353.txt",
      "filetype": "text/plain",
      "data_source": {
        "url": null,
        "version": null,
        "record_locator": {
          "id": "17353",
